    "note": "Composed by hand from the two official USCIS vocabulary lists checked in beside this file, then reviewed word by word against them. NOT model-generated - see docs/specs/english-test.md section 1.2 for why that rule exists and what it protects. USCIS publishes no sentence list to copy: M-1178 (09/17) instructs teachers to \"create as many interrogative sentences (or questions) as you can, using only the words on the list\", which is what these are. Reading sentences are interrogative and drawn only from the reading list; writing sentences are declarative and drawn only from the writing list; the two lists are never merged (M-1178: \"the lists are not the same\"). Every sentence here is re-checked on every test run by english-sentences.spec.ts - a sentence containing a word off its list fails the build rather than reaching a learner."
